## Phase 02 — Single-Owner Application Architecture

This phase defines how the application is accessed, controlled and managed.

Originally, we wanted to create a subscription-based SaaS product where multiple customers could register and use the platform.

We changed that direction.

Now the application is intended for one owner, with protected access.

Main components:

- One-owner authentication architecture.
- Secure first-owner registration.
- Restricted account creation.
- Owner-level permissions.
- Personal application settings.
- Centralized lead ownership.
- Private database access.
- Secure integration configuration.
- Removal of unnecessary customer-management infrastructure.

The application should not require customers, subscription accounts or separate workspaces.

The purpose is to make the application powerful and private without unnecessary SaaS complexity.

